169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (The volunteers shared educational materials, and each visit inspired gratitude from school staff and students. Many schools expressed their deep appreciation, highlighting the challenges of underfunding and a lack of educational resources. In particular, teachers shared their struggles with providing materials for their students, while parents affected by poverty often prioritize basic needs over school supplies. Despite these challenges, the outreach was met with overwhelming gratitude. Headmasters and headmistresses were thankful as the gifts of books and pens alleviated a significant burden for many schools.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Looking ahead, the outreach team recommends continued support for schools in Africa, as these efforts uplift students and ease the financial burdens on educators. Additionally, providing basic food items alongside educational materials would help address the issue of hunger, which many children face before coming to school. We sincerely thank our donors and volunteers for their invaluable support and prayers. May God bless Viewpoint Ministries and all those involved in this noble mission. Please support us to make more impact in 2025. You can visit info@viepointministriesinternational.org or make your donation at www.viewpointministriesinternational.org/donate)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
